&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Handwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

Handback to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/hands-room/luna/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1200 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. Your seat dir: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/hands-room/luna. Stand the house (noosphere-boot.mem), L-Prime, OODA-HA. READ-ONLY on the repo /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine; write only in your seat dir. No git writes, no suites. Web allowed; cite URLs.

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Read the common brief (/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/hands-room/brief-common.md), your own
wave one (own-wave1.md in your seat dir) and your peer's (peer-wave1.md), then the code and carriers again where you split.

You agree: one end-state model, "the session carries the hand" (road "A session wears the face and the vessel wears
none"; contract "Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session", "The door carries; the hand authorizes"); K15 bonds
lands before the hands lanes touch identity hunks; every lane red-first; identity, receipt and authorship bytes land
before the bake; I2 (the far agent's relay) runs as its own lane, scouted separately.

Settle, each with a verdict CANON (quote), DERIVED (name the house law and the code it follows, file:line) or OPERATOR
(options + one lean). Surface OPERATOR only where canon and derivation both run out.
H1. ONE LANE CUT. Sol cuts four lanes (session spine F3/F4/F5/F9/A8/W17; surfaces and holder F1/F2/F6/P13/B2; hands and
attribution F10/F11/F12; intent and effects G13). Luna cuts five (switch and contract F9/A8/W17; view and hands runtime
F1-F4/F6/F11; authored records F5/F12/P13; device and dispatch F10/B2/G13; I2). Agree ONE cut by what inherits shape:
where does the receipt (F4/F5) belong, with the session spine or the authored records? Where does P13 (per-meme
grants, the effective recipe) belong? Where does B2 (two tabs, two faces, one holder)? A lane holds a whole model; no
lane ships an interim a later lane re-cuts.
H2. WHAT MAY START NOW. K15 bonds holds the opener seed and identity hunks, `keyhive-provider`, `place-card`,
`ceremony-core`, `boot-daemon-keyhive`, `carriage-relay`, `carriage-caps`, `node-caps`. D2 (landing now) holds the tw5
island and port files, `hand-gate.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, `projection-sink.ts`. Measure: can the first hands lane
start NOW on files neither holds (session-contract, UDS, verb VM, working-slot resolver, mesh view/recipe), merging
K15's opener hunks when it lands? Or must it wait whole? Name the files and the first slice that can start.
H3. THE (FACE, NEXUS) QUESTION. The contract flags it (session-contract.mem:295): one live session names (face, Nexus) at
open, or one face session exposes both Nexuses through bounded facets? Read the proof subject, the recipe per
generation, the dial "one per (hearth, Nexus)" rule and the cabal/realm carriers. Does canon or house law settle it?
H4. THE PERSON'S JOINTS Luna named (receipt display fields; switch in place vs close and open; the long-silent device
with no clock): settle each by canon or derivation where you can; keep only true operator joints.
Then restate the agreed lanes, in order, each with its slices red-first (red, control, known positive) and the files held.

